course: dictionary
lesson: 13182
title: Fresco: paint on wet walls
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fresco is a painting made on a wall or ceiling while the plaster is still wet. The colours sink into the plaster, so they become part of the wall itself. «The artist painted a fresco of angels on the church wall.» Here fresco is a noun: it names the painting.
explain: Fresco can also mean the method, the way of painting. «She learned fresco in art class, so she could paint on the classroom wall.» The clues are wall, ceiling and wet plaster. They tell you what a fresco is, even if you have never seen one.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Visitors gaze up at the fresco on the ceiling.» Does "the painting on the wet plaster of the ceiling" still make sense there? Yes, so your meaning fits.
fact: A fresco is a painting made on wet plaster on a wall or ceiling.
fact: The colours become part of the wall, because they soak into the plaster as it dries.
fact: The plural of fresco can be frescoes or frescos.
fact: Michelangelo painted famous frescoes on the ceiling of the Sistine Chapel in Rome.
fact: Ancient frescoes can still be seen in Pompeii and on Minoan Crete, and many church walls in Europe have frescoes of Bible stories.
exercise: «The artist painted a fresco of angels on the church wall.» What is a fresco here? | A kind of stone used to build churches | A tall tower for bells | *A painting made on wet plaster on a wall | A window with coloured glass
exercise: A fresco is painted while the plaster is still what? | Frozen | Burnt | *Wet | Dusty
exercise: Which of these is a fresco? | A map of the moon | A cup of hot tea | *A painting of Bible stories on a church wall | A photo taken on a phone
exercise: Why do the colours of a fresco last so long? | *The colours soak into the plaster as it dries | The colours are washed off every year | The wall is painted again each week | The paint is glued on with tape
test: Why does a fresco become part of the wall? | Because the paint is painted on paper first | *Because the colours sink into the wet plaster as it dries | Because the wall is painted again later | Because the colours are glued on
test: Which word means the art of painting on wet plaster? | Mosaic | *Fresco | Pottery | Sculpture
exam: Michelangelo's famous fresco is on the ceiling of which building? | *The Sistine Chapel in Rome | The Tower of London | The Pyramids in Egypt | The Eiffel Tower in Paris
